        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(feishu): add chunk-idle timeout to inbound media download",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Feishu inbound media downloads that stall after the Lark SDK returns a stream body (headers/start ok, then no further chunks) would block `saveMessageResourceFeishu` forever via `saveMediaStream`'s unbounded `for await`, so inbound dispatch never produces an agent reply for that attachment.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Route every Feishu inbound `saveMediaStream` path through `saveMediaStreamWithIdleTimeout` (production floor `FEISHU_INBOUND_MEDIA_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS = 30_000`), matching Telegram's download idle floor and the WhatsApp/LINE channel pattern.\n- Idle helper lives in `extensions/feishu/src/media-chunk-idle.ts` so the oversized legacy `media.ts` does not grow past the LOC ratchet.\n- On timeout, reject with `FeishuInboundMediaTimeoutError`, call `iterator.return()`, and silence the losing `next()`.\n- Does **not** change core `saveMediaStream` / `src/media/store.ts`.\n- Does **not** touch Feishu docx URL reads (`#104663`).\n\nNo new config/env surface.\n\n## User Impact\n\n**Before:** A stalled Feishu message-resource body could hang inbound handling for that attachment indefinitely.\n\n**After:** Idle streams fail closed after 30s with a clear timeout error so the Feishu monitor loop can continue.\n\n## Evidence\n\nCompete: no open PR for `extensions/feishu/src/media.ts` chunk-idle; `#104663` is `docx.ts` only.\n\nHead: `3e369b86347a05e716d532cf0164900fd6bb5ea8`\n\n```text\n$ OPENCLAW_VITEST_MAX_WORKERS=1 node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/feishu/src/media-chunk-idle.test.ts extensions/feishu/src/media.test.ts --reporter=verbose\n\n[feishu media idle proof] timed_out=true elapsed_ms=51 chunkTimeoutMs=50 production_ms=30000\n[feishu media idle proof] production_default_ms=30000 timed_out=true\nTests  48 passed (48)\n```\n\nNegative control: never-yielding AsyncIterable without idle wrap would hang `for await`; with the 50ms floor, timeout rejects in ~51ms and `iterator.return()` is called once. Production default path advances fake timers to 30s.\n\nCI follow-up: extracted helper under LOC ratchet (`media.ts` 982 ≤ 983 baseline), fixed oxlint Promise-executor / catch-unknown issues, and avoided knip unused timeout-class exports.",
